--TEST--
`Core\Markdown\Live` gives the blocks each piece finished and the open rest, the finished parts and `finish()` join to `toHtml`'s HTML, a definition that arrives after a finished block leaves that block as text, and a push after `finish()` throws a `RuntimeError` — `rule:core-classes/markdown-chunks`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Markdown::live, Core\Markdown\Live::push, Core\Markdown\Live::finish, Core\Markdown\Update::done, Core\Markdown\Update::open
string $doc = "# Notes\n\nSee [the guide](/guide).\n\n- one\n- two\n";
Core\Markdown\Live $live = Core\Markdown::live(link: fn (string $url): ?string => "https://example.com" . $url);
string $page = "";
array<string> $pieces = ["# No", "tes\n\nSee [the gu", "ide](/guide).\n\n- one\n", "- two\n"];
foreach ($pieces as string $piece) {
    Core\Markdown\Update $update = $live->push($piece);
    string $done = Core\Html::toSource($update->done(), "the case prints each part");
    $page = $page . $done;
    echo "done: ", $done, "|\n";
    echo "open: ", Core\Html::toSource($update->open(), "the case prints each part"), "|\n";
}
string $rest = Core\Html::toSource($live->finish(), "the case prints the rest");
echo "finish: ", $rest, "|\n";
string $whole = Core\Html::toSource(
    Core\Markdown::toHtml($doc, link: fn (string $url): ?string => "https://example.com" . $url),
    "the case compares the whole",
);
echo $page . $rest == $whole ? "same as toHtml\n" : "different from toHtml\n";

// The paragraph is finished before the definition of `[the guide]` arrives.
Core\Markdown\Live $late = Core\Markdown::live();
$late->push("Read [the guide].\n\n");
echo Core\Html::toSource($late->push("More.\n\n[the guide]: /guide\n")->done(), "the case prints a part");
echo Core\Html::toSource($late->finish(), "the case prints the rest");
try {
    $late->push("more");
} catch (RuntimeError $ended) {
    echo $ended->message, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--
done: |
open: <h1>No</h1>
|
done: |
open: <h1>Notes</h1>
<p>See [the gu</p>
|
done: <h1>Notes</h1>
<p>See <a href="https://example.com/guide">the guide</a>.</p>
|
open: <ul>
<li>one</li>
</ul>
|
done: |
open: <ul>
<li>one</li>
<li>two</li>
</ul>
|
finish: <ul>
<li>one</li>
<li>two</li>
</ul>
|
same as toHtml
<p>Read [the guide].</p>
<p>More.</p>
Core\Markdown\Live::push(): this document has ended, because `finish()` was called or a callback threw an error. Create a new one with `Core\Markdown::live()`.
